From 5a606ee5c11002c21b2870f8ae1214fcdfab000b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kevinbrar2024 <kevinbrar2024@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 06:21:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Check player loss only after a resolution or replacement
 finishes (CR 704.3, CR 704.4, CR 614.1c)

A land's "as this land enters, choose a basic land type. Then you may pay
2 life" taken at exactly 2 life left its controller at 0 life with the
land-type choice still open. The terminal player-loss safety net ran
state-based actions inside that event; eliminating the player then tried to
abandon the resolution carrier with the post-replacement frame on top and
panicked.

The same net also ran at every prompt a resolving spell or ability raised,
so a player at 0 life in the middle of a resolution lost before the rest of
it happened, even when a later instruction gained that player life.
State-based actions are checked when a player would receive priority
(CR 704.3) and pay no attention to what happens during a resolution
(CR 704.4).

The net now waits while a resolution carrier is held or any frame of the
resolution stack is a replacement's unfinished instructions. It still runs
for prompts outside both, such as a cleanup discard.

Two existing tests pinned the mid-resolution loss and now assert the
rules outcome: the payer at 0 life makes the payment and is judged when
priority is next given, and the loss after Yenna's host prompt is processed
after the scry that ends that resolution.

Co-Authored-By: Devin AI <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
